{"tool_name":"bis-snp","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"bis-snp","identifiers":["biotools:bis-snp","doi:10.1186/gb-2012-13-7-r61"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Bisulfite-seq/nome-seq snps & cytosine methylation caller","home_url":"http://people.csail.mit.edu/dnaase/bissnp2011/","keywords":["Animals","DNA","DNA Methylation","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Mice","Models, Genetic","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Genotype and phenotype","Epigenetics","Sequencing"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"bis-snp","home":"http://people.csail.mit.edu/dnaase/bissnp2011/","license":"MIT","summary":"A package based on the Genome Analysis Toolkit map-reduce framework for genotyping in bisulfite treated massively parallel sequencing on Illumina platform. It uses bayesian inference with either manually specified or automatically estimated methylation probabilities of different cytosine context(not only CpG, CHH, CHG in Bisulfite-seq, but also GCH et.al. in other bisulfite treated sequencing) to determine genotypes and methylation levels simultaneously.","addition_date":"2017-01-13T13:13:49Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:35:57.427325Z","tool_type":["Suite"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bis-snp","credit":[{"email":"bberman@usc.edu","name":"Benjamin P Berman","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://people.csail.mit.edu/dnaase/bissnp2011/BisSNP-UserGuide-latest.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Bisulfite mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3186"},{"term":"Methylation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3204"},{"term":"SNP detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"Bis-SNP","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"seqwiki_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/gb-2012-13-7-r61","metadata":{"abstract":"Bisulfite treatment of DNA followed by high-throughput sequencing (Bisulfite-seq) is an important method for studying DNA methylation and epigenetic gene regulation, yet current software tools do not adequately address single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs). Identifying SNPs is important for accurate quantification of methylation levels and for identification of allele-specific epigenetic events such as imprinting. We have developed a model-based bisulfite SNP caller, Bis-SNP, that results in substantially better SNP calls than existing methods, thereby improving methylation estimates. At an average 30\u00d7 genomic coverage, Bis-SNP correctly identified 96% of SNPs using the default high-stringency settings. The open-source package is available at http://epigenome.usc.edu/publicationdata/bissnp2011. \u00a9 2012 Liu et al.; licensee BioMed Central Ltd.","authors":[{"name":"Berman B.P."},{"name":"Laird P.W."},{"name":"Liu Y."},{"name":"Siegmund K.D."}],"citationCount":197,"date":"2012-07-11T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"Bis-SNP: Combined DNA methylation and SNP calling for Bisulfite-seq data"},"pmcid":"PMC3491382","pmid":"22784381"}],"topic":[{"term":"Epigenetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3295"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Bis-SNP","home":"https://bio.tools/bis-snp","license":"MIT","summary":"A package based on the Genome Analysis Toolkit map-reduce framework for genotyping in bisulfite treated massively parallel sequencing on Illumina platform. It uses bayesian inference with either manually specified or automatically estimated methylation probabilities of different cytosine context(not only CpG, CHH, CHG in Bisulfite-seq, but also GCH et.al. in other bisulfite treated sequencing) to determine genotypes and methylation levels simultaneously.","too